i.github.com/users/Eonis48/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eonis48/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eonis48/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T12:15:16Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T12:15:16Z","body":"Hello,\n\nThank you for the clarification regarding the model.\n\nI understand that I am currently using ChatGPT Codex 5.2 (Beta), and I accept that beta models may occasionally behave unpredictably. However, the recurring issue I am experiencing goes beyond normal beta instability.\n\nAfter very long processing times, the system marks the request as “complete” but returns no output — while still consuming credits. This has been happening repeatedly (almost weekly), resulting in lost time and unnecessary credit usage.\n\nEven for a beta model, there should be safeguards in place:\n\nIf generation fails or produces empty output, credits should not be deducted\n\nThe system should not mark the task as “complete” when no output is returned\n\nThere should be a visible warning if a model is currently unstable\n\nI am fully open to testing beta systems, but predictable failure handling and fair credit management are essential.\n\nCould you please clarify:\n\nWhether empty completions are a known issue with Codex 5.2 Beta\n\nIf credit refunds are possible in these cases\n\nWhether improvements to failure detection are planned\n\nI appreciate your support and look forward to a concrete resolution.\n\nBest regards,\nUlaş Çakır\nulascakir@gmail.com","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/comments/3966243181/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/comments/3966276159","html_url":"https://github.com/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/2296#i